    <briefdescription>
<para>Structured log-sampling and rate-limiting interface. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>All methods that make or record a sampling decision are noexcept; log sampling must never throw or abort the calling thread.</para>
<para>Contract: <ref refid="classthemis_1_1utils_1_1_i_structured_log_sampler_1a644b50af6f72d23b0abf880ee3fc428a" kindref="member">shouldSample()</ref> MUST return true for any entry with eventClass == <ref refid="namespacethemis_1_1utils_1ab5e8042d31a3cddab9b1c845096e068fa2fae32629d4ef4fc6341f1751b405e45" kindref="member">EventClass::Security</ref>, regardless of the current rate. Conforming implementations should enforce this via a short-circuit check before consulting the rate limiter. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
